From 94a9a05e81df8ceeebec1647a91cad9011c5cd74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 08:32:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] um: arm64: default to 16 KB pages

A guest page is a host mmap(), so the guest's page size cannot be smaller
than the host's: a 4 KB guest cannot boot on a 16 KB host, and fails by
hanging rather than by saying so. A 16 KB guest runs on both -- four host
pages per guest page on a 4 KB host, one-to-one on a 16 KB one.

So 16 KB is the only setting that covers the whole fleet, and Android 15
and later ship 16 KB kernels. The cost is internal fragmentation on 4 KB
devices, a few percent of memory. The alternative costs not booting on
current hardware. CONFIG_PAGE_SIZE_4KB remains available for builds that
know their host and want the memory back.

Verified on a purpose-built 16 KB arm64 run domain: 16 KB guest on 16 KB
host boots and runs Alpine from ubd0, and 16 KB guest on 4 KB host passes
the same gates as the 4 KB build.

Signed-off-by: Oleksii Zakharov <contact@zalexdev.com>
---
 arch/um/configs/arm64_defconfig | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/um/configs/arm64_defconfig b/arch/um/configs/arm64_defconfig
index 2adabee796802..f06c59f30ff91 100644
--- a/arch/um/configs/arm64_defconfig
+++ b/arch/um/configs/arm64_defconfig
@@ -1,3 +1,18 @@
+#
+# 16 KB pages by default.
+#
+# A guest page is a host mmap(), so the guest's page size cannot be smaller than
+# the host's -- a 4 KB guest simply cannot boot on a 16 KB host, and does so by
+# hanging rather than by failing. A 16 KB guest runs on both: four host pages
+# per guest page on a 4 KB host, one-to-one on a 16 KB one.
+#
+# So 16 KB is the only setting that covers the whole fleet, and Android 15 and
+# later ship 16 KB kernels. The cost is internal fragmentation on 4 KB devices,
+# a few percent of memory; the alternative costs not booting at all on current
+# hardware. CONFIG_PAGE_SIZE_4KB remains available for memory-constrained
+# builds that know their host.
+#
+CONFIG_PAGE_SIZE_16KB=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y
 CONFIG_RD_GZIP=y
 CONFIG_RD_XZ=y
